  "saveImpact": [
    "Changes the published schemas of aspersorium and sacristan_table, even if IDs stay unchanged. Requires a new version and explicit migration; not a drop-in update.",
    "Back up raw registry dynamic-property values, not parsed snapshots: parseDockedRegistryShard sanitizes fields and normalizes entries. Preserve item instance ID, charges, cosmetic, spray profile, unknown future data and dimension/location mapping; report occupied-without-snapshot and empty-with-snapshot mismatches without repairing them.",
    "Export/backup must happen with the old decoder before swapping schemas. Migration of loaded blocks alone misses unloaded chunks, structures and commands.",
    "Any old empty block with nonzero cosmetic is explicitly normalized to empty/cosmetic0; runtime already writes that state on undocking. Water pair(9,8) is retained unchanged as an existing alias of capacity16.",
    "Rollback requires the paired old pack, world and registry snapshot. Reinstalling the old pack alone after state conversion is not safe."
  ],
  "requiredFutureTests": [
    "Actual adapter transitions: place/dock/undock/recolor/fill/load/break; all rotations and all cosmetics; no item or water duplication.",
    "Partial-write injection at registry, inventory and block permutation writes, plus session cancellation, contention and unknown chunks.",
    "Migration dry run and inverse snapshot roundtrip before any world copy is opened.",
    "Native Content Log, save/reopen and physical smoke by the user."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "208-state combined margin is small, not a generous performance or compatibility reserve. Other add-ons consume additional states.",
    "This intentionally extends schema work to Aspergillum. Parent has authorized only read-only analysis, not implementation.",
    "No Minecraft validation, benchmark, live transaction test or automatic world migration was performed.",
    "The artwork is from a prior checked build with byte-identical generator, customization catalog and base geometries; input SHA-256 hashes are recorded."
  ],
